        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "For the triangle with \\(AB=13\\text{ cm}\\), \\(BC=14\\text{ cm}\\), and \\(AC=15\\text{ cm}\\), \\(BD\\) is perpendicular to \\(AC\\). Find \\(BD\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "From Heron's formula, \\(S=84\\text{ cm}^2\\). Since \\(BD\\perp AC\\), \\(S=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AC\\cdot BD=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot15\\cdot BD\\). Therefore, \\(BD=\\frac{56}{5}\\text{ cm}\\).",
